build 23: EXPERIMENT -- a song from a famous equation (23 of them: y = mx + b, quadratic, sine, bell curve, logistic, damped oscillator, Fourier square wave, harmonic series, golden ratio, Fibonacci, Pythagorean triples as chords, inverse square, exponential growth, Weierstrass, tangent, Euler's formula, Lissajous, rose, cardioid, Archimedean spiral, heart, butterfly, Riemann zeta), written as in the textbook; MUSICAL mode reads it as the melody's shape snapped to a key with bass, harmony and drums; WILD mode sings the raw maths; right-click picks the equation and mode; 4 scenes that build, the last with new numbers; Greek letters typeset; plane(a, b, ...) draws a and b, the rest only sing. build 22: DRAG -- a button at the top opens a page that splits the song into its parts (Kick, Snare, Clap, Hi-hat, Open hat, Bass, Lead, Arp, Pad ... worked out from the voice names and how each line plays), each a WAV and a MIDI handle to drag into the DAW (drums on channel 10 as GM notes), plus the whole song (mix WAV, all-parts MIDI) and every part at once; files saved in Music/Ghost Graph/Exports; WAVs render in the background. Tempo on the main page: BPM readout (drag, scroll or double-click to type) with a SYNC switch -- shows the DAW's tempo greyed when following it; SYNC greyed in the standalone app. build 21: Track 7, the zeta video -- y = plane(zre(u), zim(u)), u = 4x + 32: the Riemann zeta function on the critical line, zeta(1/2 + iu), drawn on a new Re / Im plane view (the path grows from u = 0 to 64, a blue dot at its head), typeset as y = { Re zeta(1/2 + iu)  Im zeta(1/2 + iu) }; new zre / zim functions; new SILVER look (black ink, blue dot, soft grey crumpled paper), which the track switches to; its two voices sing the real and imaginary parts a fifth per unit around D2 on a saw, timed to the video (3 u a second, measured from the dot). build 20: EDIT changes the real formulas in place - no more editK lines (a moved kick reads kick = {1 < x < 1.6: at(...), 0 < x < 0.6: none, h < 0.3: ...}, a held note {-6 < x < 10: -5/12, -8 < x < 8: none, -1}); click a note and its piece of the math gets a box and an arrow (plus its entry in y = [...]); right-click a note: Copy / Delete, right-click the paper: Paste (lands where you click, greyed out until something is copied; Cmd+C / Cmd+V too); Cmd+click to pick several notes, Cmd+drag a box round them, Cmd+A for all, then grab any one and they all move together (one UNDO). build 19: dragging much quicker (the text box catches up when you let go). build 18: click a note then Delete removes it (UNDO brings it back); dragging about 9x quicker. build 17: black typing cursor on the light looks. build 16: opens in the TI 84 look; hover tips drawn in each look; REDO next to UNDO. build 15: TI 84 look redone as a green calculator LCD (monospaced type, dotted grid, key row with EDIT); WINE lettering. Version 1.9.0. build 14: Ghost Graph lettering at the top of PAPER, CHROMA, INK and TI 84 (Brandon's art). Version 1.8.0. build 13: shows "Ghost Graph · v1 beta" in the control bar; CREDITS.txt inside the plugin. Version 1.7.1. build 12: EDIT button (by the equations) - type in the math AND drag notes on the graph: grab the middle to move a note in time and pitch (snaps to 1/16 beat and semitones; Alt = finer), grab either end to make it shorter or longer, or pull an end up or down to tilt it into a diagonal. Every drag rewrites the math: the voice becomes editK = {...} with at(...) and none, and dragging the same note again updates it; UNDO undoes drags. In EDIT the whole of every line shows (faint ahead of the playhead), the note under the mouse lights up with handles, and the scene loops. New in the math: at(f, t) and none. All five looks checked normal and in EDIT; typing over watercolour gets a paper card. Version 1.7.0. build 11: TI 84 look tidied - the screen frame clears the scene name, the equations panel clears the first line. Version 1.6.2. build 10: checked every track against its video (frames side by side, and the notes the equations predict found in each video's audio, with a wrong-key control). Fixes: Track 5 tuned to E3 (measured; was A3); Track 1's scenes each run at their own speed like the first video (scene lengths 12.8, 12.1, 11.0, 15.0, 14.0, 12.0 s); the graph keeps the videos' fixed -2.5..2.5 window instead of zooming to fit; steep drum hits are drawn as one stroke (lines only break where the function really jumps). Version 1.6.1. build 9: Track 6 - the burgundy video, all nine scenes equation for equation (80 BPM, soft saw on D3); up to 12 scenes now. Two new looks: WINE (the burgundy video: cream lines, orange dots on wine-red crumpled paper) and TI 84 (a graphing calculator: black body, the graph on a light LCD with a status bar, Y1-Y6 in calculator colours, the equations on a dark panel, the y= window zoom trace graph keys). INK ghost: the circle under the mouth removed. Control bar rearranged into two rows so nothing overlaps. Version 1.6.0. build 8: INK ghost - no arms; bigger and placed like Brandon's picture: the whole head up on the right in orange and teal, the deep indigo body flowing down and to the left into the hem. Version 1.5.2. build 7: the INK look's watercolour is now a ghost - round head, a body that bellies out and flows into a wavy hem with a curling tail, wispy arms, two hollow eyes holding the dials, a little "o" mouth, drips falling off the hem; paint that strays outside the ghost goes faint so the shape reads. Version 1.5.1. build 6: LOOK button with two new looks from Brandon's pictures (painted in code): CHROMA - a rainbow watercolour splash across a white page with ink ripples, an atom, stars, a sound wave and math signs; INK - indigo, teal, purple and burnt-orange watercolour pouring down cream paper with binary rain, graph-paper grids, dials, drips and a bundle of waves. On those looks every voice gets its own ink colour with a paper halo, dots are rimmed in the voice colour, the math gets a soft glow and dark ink; PAPER is the videos' look as before. The look is saved with the project. Version 1.5.0. build 5: GENERATE rebuilt to write songs the way the videos are written - each song follows one video's blueprint (Drift, Riff house, Breaks, Cosine song, Acid) with new music: evenly spread (Euclidean) rhythms, digit-number riffs that answer themselves bar to bar, six-voice chords with smooth voice leading and the scoop into each chord, glides into the next chord, phrase-end fills, every note in the song's key; each style sets its video's wave, tuning and tempo range. Right-click GENERATE (or ... menu) to pick the style. Measured against the videos: same clash, busyness and repetition. Version 1.4.0. build 4 (Tracks 2 and 3 at the videos' loudness): looks and sounds like the videos. Sound measured from the videos themselves: y = 0 is A3 (220 Hz; the first video D3), each track gets its own wave (Track 1 SOFT SAW, Tracks 2-3 ROUND, Tracks 4-5 SQUARE, Track 5 a little darker), every voice at the same fixed level, dry; voices named hats are a metallic hi-hat and snare / clap / rim are noise, like the videos (KIT switch). Look: the videos' colours (orange lines, yellow-amber math, cream dots), lines drawn only up to the playhead, grid every 2 along x, wide margins, big math that scales with the window, crumpled paper with the fold across the middle; the controls hide while you watch and come back when the mouse is near the bottom. GENERATE: gliding chords and acid lines added. Version 1.3.0. build 3: TRACKS - all five reference videos in the plugin, every scene with its own equations at its own tempo (the first video, plus the 5-, 8-, 7- and 6-scene videos you sent). GENERATE writes a brand-new track of our own in the same math (intro, groove, full, break, full; one key and groove; bit-pattern drums and bass, digit-number melodies, scale-walk chords, cosine melodies, risers); ... menu: generate just this scene, undo GENERATE. New in the math: != and y = outline(...). Version 1.2.0. build 2: the six scenes are now the reference video's own equations, equation for equation (and laid out like it: the y list two to a row), a bare {condition} works like Desmos (1 where true, silent elsewhere), TEMPO starts at 75 like the video, the cheat sheet hides behind ? so the equations get the full width. Version 1.1.0. build 1: Ghost Graph 1.0.0 - music written as equations: 6 scenes, live graphs with glowing playheads, typeset math you can click and edit, SYNC / PLAY / CHAIN / KEYS, 4 waves, TUNE GLIDE TONE SPACE WIDTH VOLUME
